        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding: work order identified; late-event determination blocked\n\nThe records identify the September manufacturing order ending in **1070** as:\n\n| Item | Verified value |\n|---|---|\n| Manufacturing order | **MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Work-order ID | **WO-2025-09-004** |\n| Operation | Modine Racine, DeKoven |\n| Product | Cooler Plate Pack |\n| Cost period | **Sep-25 — PER-COST-2025-09** |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n\nThe source timestamp does not specify a time zone.\n\n### Event-specific evidence is unavailable\n\nThe accessible records contain work orders and cost periods but **no cost-event rows**. The assigned supporting ledger repeatedly returned **“Supporting input was not staged for this assignment.”** Authorized shared evidence did not supply the missing event details.\n\nConsequently, I cannot substantiate the **source transaction, amount, exact event-created time, lateness, or recorded accounting status**. This is an evidence gap—not evidence that no late event occurred. Lateness would be calculated as:\n\n`(event-created time − 2025-09-30T18:00:00) ÷ 60 seconds`\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\n\nOracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B, **“Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” PDF page 233 / printed page 225**, states that:\n\n- Newly created transactions falling in or before a Pending Close period are **not staged in Cost Accounting or Receipt Accounting**; processing waits until the period is closed or reopened.\n- Transactions entered before Pending Close continue to be processed, even if in error.\n- **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments** continue to be processed after Pending Close.\n\n**Conclusion:** An ordinary, non-exempt transaction newly created after **2025-09-30T18:00:00** should be held while the period remains Pending Close. Whether this work order had such an event—and whether its recorded status is consistent with that policy—**remains undetermined until the original event ledger is available**.\n\nNo database records were changed. The evidence-limited audit and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_6094246c1b0f/audit-report.json`; the submitted report remains marked **needs evidence**.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
      "phase": "final_answer"
    }
